cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GDS-ParT in research or a report, please cite it as below."
title: "GDS-ParT: Gated Dual-Stream Particle Transformer for jet tagging"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Avinash Chandra
    family-names: Gupta
    alias: Avinashistoocool
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-30
repository-code: "https://github.com/Avinashistoocool/Gated-Dual-Stream-Particle-Transformer"
url: "https://avinashistoocool.github.io/Gated-Dual-Stream-Particle-Transformer/"
abstract: >-
  GDS-ParT is a PyTorch transformer for jet tagging on the JetClass benchmark. Instead of only adding
  pairwise kinematics to the attention logits as in the Particle Transformer (ParT), it keeps a particle
  stream and a pairwise relation stream, aggregates each particle's relations into a summary, and maps
  the summary to identity-initialised gates (1 + tanh) that rescale the query and key channels before the
  dot product. The reported v2 configuration combines these gates with a ParT-style pairwise bias and
  class-attention pooling. With 2.07M parameters and 10 million training jets it reaches 0.8484 test
  accuracy and 0.9853 macro AUC on a balanced one-million-jet JetClass test subset. The repository
  includes a memory-efficient data pipeline, training and ablation scripts, a pipeline check against the
  official ParT checkpoint, and a technical report with the full mathematics.
keywords:
  - particle physics
  - high-energy physics
  - jet tagging
  - JetClass
  - transformer
  - attention
  - gating
  - Particle Transformer
  - machine learning
  - PyTorch
